A||N||4||MontanaFiero||Where does THIS go?||||5||
Z||000000||MontanaFiero||09-05-2001||03:24 AM||||Remember, when I got this car a lot of things were missing... I have plugs left over...these two are by the coil. They do NOT go to the temp sensor, as that sensor and plug have been moved to the other head. <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/fierofotos/plug3.jpg"> <P>This plug is by the EGR selenoid, or somewhere in that area.  Also, is this hose supposed to plug into the EGR selenoid?? If not where-- and what does?  <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/fierofotos/plug2.jpg"> <P>And now... I seem to have forgotten how to put these back on. They are the engine strut braces. Can someone (with their motor accessible) snap a picture so i can use it as a guide? <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/fierofotos/strut.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Wolfhound||09-05-2001||07:45 AM||||Photo 1= both to distributor base.<BR>photo 2= hose attaches to steel vacumn line on the trunk side of engine compartment.<BR>The opening on the EGR solenoid is open to atmosphere. pre recall it attached to the piping across the firewall.<BR>The plug goes to the second temp sensor below the thermostat housing. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||09-05-2001||08:18 AM||||I agree with Wolfhound, and...<P>Photo 3:<BR>Both brackets go on the front of the engine, and the 2 attach to each other.  Since your engine's on a stand, I'm using "engine" directions (e.g. - "front" means water pump end, etc.), not "car/body" directions.   <P>Bracket on right hand side of photo attaches to front of left head, and the skinny curved part arches over the water pump.  Attachment to head takes 3 fasteners (15mm socket), all into the front side of the left head..  Center fastener is a stud; the other 2 are bolts.  BTW, oil pressure sender bracket attaches under the leftmost bolt.<P>Bracket on left hand side of photo goes on top of right head; the "clevis" opens to the right, to receive the "dogbone" strut.  Attaches to right head with (2) bolts (15mm socket)- one into top of right head near lower edge of valve cover, and the other into front of right head.  Attach to the end of the skinny part of the other bracket mentioned above (which has a welded-on nut in the end), using a bolt through the hole in the base of the clevis (15mm socket).   <P>Happy wrenching    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">      <BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 09-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GTZ34||09-05-2001||08:59 AM||||Montana a couple of observations beyond what you posted...  If that is a knock sensor on the side of the eng block in the 1st picture, you won't need that.  If it is an oil sender, I would suggest using the original fiero setup due to heat.  Also, your temp sender is missing.  It goes where the plug is on corner of the head in the 1st picture.  And you should also get a Fiero dipstick and tube as it will hard to check it under the decklid lip.  Disregard this if you have already addressed them, I am trying to save you time.  GL!||||reg||1
Z||000004||MontanaFiero||09-05-2001||10:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87GTZ34:<BR><B>Montana a couple of observations beyond what you posted...  If that is a knock sensor on the side of the eng block in the 1st picture, you won't need that.  If it is an oil sender, I would suggest using the original fiero setup due to heat.  Also, your temp sender is missing.  It goes where the plug is on corner of the head in the 1st picture.  And you should also get a Fiero dipstick and tube as it will hard to check it under the decklid lip.  Disregard this if you have already addressed them, I am trying to save you time.  GL!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Yeah, I have a dipstick coming, and I couldn't get the plug out, so I moved the sensor to the other head. (Now its located in the back where it's totally inaccessible). There was already a sensor there.  That is a knock sensor you are refering to. Can I just leave it there? As for the oil pressure sensor...  check this out <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013249.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013249.html</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
